# {{.Title}}

Built with [Aemeath](https://github.com/naufalraism/aemeath).

## Run it

```bash
aemeath dev{{if .Web}} --ts-out web/src/api{{end}}        # the API with hot reload (http://localhost:3000)
go test ./...      # run the tests
```
{{if .Web}}
The React app lives in `web/`. In a second terminal:

```bash
cd web
npm install
npm run dev        # http://localhost:5173, proxies /api to the Go server
```

`aemeath dev --ts-out web/src/api` rewrites the typed client, the Zod schemas and the React Query hooks in `web/src/api/` every time the Go code changes, so the frontend always matches the API.

For production, `npm run build` in `web/` fills `web/dist`, which the Go server serves at `/`.
{{else}}
- API docs: http://localhost:3000/docs
- Typed TypeScript client: http://localhost:3000/client.ts
{{end}}
## Add more

```bash
aemeath generate api Product{{if .DB}} --db{{end}}   # CRUD handlers + tests, registered in main.go for you
aemeath generate job SendEmail                      # a background job with a retrying runner
aemeath generate docker                             # Dockerfile + docker-compose.yml
aemeath ts --out web/src/api                        # TypeScript client, Zod schemas, React Query hooks
```
{{if .DB}}
The database is SQLite (`app.db`, ignored by git). Each generated resource creates its own table when the server starts.
{{end}}
